led.</p><h2>Information you provide</h2><p>If you contact the site, information you choose to send may be used to respond to your message or review a correction.</p><h2>Technical logs</h2><p>Hosting providers may process technical data such as IP addresses, browser details, requested URLs and timestamps for security and reliability. Check the hosting provider's current policy for details.</p><h2>Analytics and cookies</h2><p>This site uses Google Analytics 4 with measurement ID <code>G-3RNLG473FS</code> to understand site usage, such as page views, referring pages, browser and device context, and interactions. Google Analytics may use cookies or similar technologies and may process data on Google's systems. Review <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/6004245">Google Analytics' data safeguards and privacy information</a> for more detail. You can limit cookies through your browser settings. Where applicable law requires consent for analytics storage or similar technologies, the site operator must implement an appropriate consent mechanism before using them.</p><h2>Advertising</h2><p>Third-party advertising is not described as active by this notice. If advertising is added later, this policy must be updated to identify the relevant providers, explain their use of cookies or similar technologies, and describe any consent choices required for visitors.</p><h2>External links and contact</h2><p>Third-party sources have their own privacy practices. For privacy questions, use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. This policy should be reviewed whenever the site's services or applicable requirements change.</p></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="container footer-main"><div class="footer-brand"><a class="brand brand-footer" href="/"><span class="brand-mark">F<span>+</span></span><span class="brand-words"><strong>World Food Crisis</strong><small>Facts before fear.</